<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, our work presented Neural Riemannian Motion Fields (NRMF), a novel framework for modeling 3D human motion while rigorously respecting the underlying geometry of articulated motions. By decomposing motion into its constituent components—pose, transition, and acceleration—and representing these as the zero-level sets of dedicated neural distance fields, NRMF acts as a strong inductive bias bridging the gap between learning and physical modeling of human motion. Our proposed projection and geometric integration algorithms help ensuring temporal consistency and robustness against noise and enable versatile applications ranging from motion denoising and in-betweening to test-time optimization for mesh recovery. Extensive experiments on diverse benchmarks consistently confirm that NRMF outperforms existing methods, delivering enhanced accuracy and more lifelike trajectories.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Limitation &amp; future work</h4>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our iterative updates can incur significant runtime leading to minutes for processing a sequence of <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;1\mathrm{min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;1\mathrm{min}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, our projected-integrators lack rigorous theoretical understanding, preventing us from certifying their optimality. As such, our work leaves ample room for future study. <em id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Learning-to-optimize</em> can be an effective future direction, while principled sampling algorithms such as <em id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Riemannian Langevin MCMC</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> can be employed as integrators.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Acknowledgement</h4>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">T. Birdal acknowledges support from the Engineering and Physical Sciences Research Council [grant EP/X011364/1].
T. Birdal was supported by a UKRI Future Leaders Fellowship [grant MR/Y018818/1].</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
